00:32:02.440 --> 00:32:04.090
I think most people raise money,

00:32:04.090 --> 00:32:05.973
or with high interest rates,

00:32:05.973 --> 00:32:09.360
because they want shit faster.

00:32:09.360 --> 00:32:10.653
I want stuff slower.

00:32:13.870 --> 00:32:16.170
The bigger the ambition, the more

00:32:16.170 --> 00:32:17.570
patience you have to deploy.

00:32:20.210 --> 00:32:22.433
So, that worked out.

00:32:22.433 --> 00:32:24.730
A lot of this shit, I
didn't realize at the time.

00:32:24.730 --> 00:32:26.270
The reason I talk about
a lot of this stuff now

00:32:26.270 --> 00:32:27.740
is like, it's hindsight.

00:32:27.740 --> 00:32:29.510
I can look back and be like, oh.

00:32:29.510 --> 00:32:31.830
So much came to me natural, you know?

00:32:31.830 --> 00:32:34.600
But, I didn't have to
deal with interest rates

00:32:34.600 --> 00:32:36.450
cause I never looked to borrow money.

00:32:37.570 --> 00:32:39.370
I was willing to eat...

00:32:39.370 --> 00:32:41.540
When I started Vayner
Medium, my company now,

00:32:41.540 --> 00:32:42.720
it's gonna be a billion dollar company.

00:32:42.720 --> 00:32:46.230
It started in a conference room
in somebody else's company.

00:32:46.230 --> 00:32:48.122
Cause I didn't wanna pay rent.

00:32:48.122 --> 00:32:49.730
Because I wasn't worried about

00:32:49.730 --> 00:32:51.750
people coming to see a fancy office.

00:32:51.750 --> 00:32:53.650
People are just fronting all the time.

00:32:56.400 --> 00:32:57.233
Yes sir.

00:33:00.070 --> 00:33:04.200
- [Audience Member] How'd
you keep yourself believing

00:33:04.200 --> 00:33:05.850
that it was gonna work out?

00:33:05.850 --> 00:33:08.300
- I never doubted when
I made the investment.

00:33:08.300 --> 00:33:09.970
I'm not writing some kid a 25,

00:33:09.970 --> 00:33:13.023
50 thousand dollar check
cause I doubt it, you know?

00:33:14.440 --> 00:33:17.540
Unfortunately, in that
game, six months later,

00:33:17.540 --> 00:33:19.990
forget about doubt, you regret it.

00:33:19.990 --> 00:33:21.150
The biggest thing I learned was

00:33:21.150 --> 00:33:23.200
there was a lot of fake entrepreneurs.

00:33:23.200 --> 00:33:24.450
The biggest mistake I made was

00:33:24.450 --> 00:33:27.430
I was coaching, investing, and thinking,

00:33:27.430 --> 00:33:29.083
as if that person was me.

00:33:30.070 --> 00:33:32.550
And I learned, like you
know, I like the idea,

00:33:32.550 --> 00:33:34.510
I could see how they could do it,

00:33:34.510 --> 00:33:35.880
but they weren't me.

00:33:35.880 --> 00:33:37.715
Because I'd look on their Instagram

00:33:37.715 --> 00:33:41.470
and they're like at the
beach on Friday afternoon.

00:33:41.470 --> 00:33:42.820
And the first time I see that photo,

00:33:42.820 --> 00:33:44.700
I'm like, I'm dead.

00:33:44.700 --> 00:33:46.670
Because they weren't even making money.

00:33:46.670 --> 00:33:48.360
They borrowed money.

00:33:48.360 --> 00:33:50.140
And the audacity's enormous.

00:33:50.140 --> 00:33:51.607
People go out of business,
they write me an email,

00:33:51.607 --> 00:33:55.517
"Dear Gary, sorry to
inform you, looks like

00:33:55.517 --> 00:33:57.817
"we'll be closing up
shop, our app has failed,

00:33:57.817 --> 00:33:59.957
"we have seven thousand dollars left

00:33:59.957 --> 00:34:03.597
"that's entitled to you, you know?

00:34:03.597 --> 00:34:07.027
"We're really sorry, but
good news, good news,

00:34:07.027 --> 00:34:10.087
"I learned a lot and in the future,

00:34:10.087 --> 00:34:11.540
"maybe we can do something."

00:34:11.540 --> 00:34:14.100
And I would reply and be like, good news?

00:34:14.100 --> 00:34:16.649
You lost my hundred thousand
dollars motherfucker.

00:34:16.649 --> 00:34:17.482
(audience laughter)

00:34:17.482 --> 00:34:19.850
And there's just so much of
that entitlement you know?

00:34:19.850 --> 00:34:21.740
In the last three, four
years, I've gotten out.

00:34:21.740 --> 00:34:23.960
I've been building my business

00:34:23.960 --> 00:34:27.493
because there's so much fake
entrepreneurship in the game.

00:34:30.378 --> 00:34:31.402
My guy.

00:34:31.402 --> 00:34:34.485
(low speaking voice)

00:34:36.810 --> 00:34:38.120
It's my life.

00:34:38.120 --> 00:34:40.470
Every day, it's running through my desk.

00:34:40.470 --> 00:34:43.280
I'm seeing pictures, I
have a full time guy.

00:34:43.280 --> 00:34:46.510
Phil Toronto, on my team,
who's looking at businesses.

00:34:46.510 --> 00:34:49.500
But I'm running a very
big business right now,

00:34:49.500 --> 00:34:51.330
where I have an office in London,

00:34:51.330 --> 00:34:54.070
I'm opening up one in Brazil
and Singapore next year,

00:34:54.070 --> 00:34:56.100
so I'm so busy on my own thing right now

00:34:56.100 --> 00:34:57.310
because I'm not investing as much,

00:34:57.310 --> 00:34:59.503
cause I think there's a lot of fake stuff.

00:34:59.503 --> 00:35:01.130
(low speaking voice)

00:35:01.130 --> 00:35:02.350
Yeah, I have a parent company

00:35:02.350 --> 00:35:04.900
called VaynerX, I have VaynerMedia.

00:35:04.900 --> 00:35:07.830
I bought a women's media
site called Pure Wow,

00:35:07.830 --> 00:35:11.370
started a dude site called 137 PM,

00:35:11.370 --> 00:35:13.193
so I'm putting in work.

00:35:16.210 --> 00:35:17.532
Yeah.

00:35:17.532 --> 00:35:20.615
(low speaking voice)

00:35:21.930 --> 00:35:23.363
I played Madden in college.

00:35:24.730 --> 00:35:26.750
You know and listen, that's
not what you should be doing.

00:35:26.750 --> 00:35:28.580
If I was lucky enough to
come to a place like this,

00:35:28.580 --> 00:35:30.500
and I had those skills, to
get this kind of education,

00:35:30.500 --> 00:35:31.580
I would have.

00:35:31.580 --> 00:35:33.123
But that wasn't who I was.

00:35:35.300 --> 00:35:37.140
I just was not a student, my guy.

00:35:37.140 --> 00:35:39.210
Like just, I didn't have it in me.

00:35:39.210 --> 00:35:40.740
You know?

00:35:40.740 --> 00:35:42.380
Even now, Marcus is standing over there,

00:35:42.380 --> 00:35:44.280
my Chief of Staff, like he's gotta

00:35:44.280 --> 00:35:47.060
keep me focused on like everything.

00:35:47.060 --> 00:35:48.293
Self awareness man.

00:35:49.430 --> 00:35:50.263
Right?

00:35:50.263 --> 00:35:51.480
Even on the field for a lot of you.

00:35:51.480 --> 00:35:52.740
Self awareness.

00:35:52.740 --> 00:35:55.040
Know what you can and can't do.

00:35:55.040 --> 00:35:56.293
That really matters.

00:35:57.790 --> 00:35:59.800
So, and it was tough man.

00:35:59.800 --> 00:36:01.510
You know like, when I was coming up,

00:36:01.510 --> 00:36:03.290
entrepreneurship was nothing.

00:36:03.290 --> 00:36:04.590
Now, everybody wants
to be an entrepreneur,

00:36:04.590 --> 00:36:05.823
now I'm cool, you know?

00:36:07.706 --> 00:36:09.760
But like, it was tough.

00:36:09.760 --> 00:36:12.213
But I just couldn't
hear anything, you know?

00:36:15.550 --> 00:36:16.410
Yes sir.

00:36:16.410 --> 00:36:17.740
- [Audience Member] Do you believe

00:36:17.740 --> 00:36:19.903
in taking breaks and vacations?

00:36:21.673 --> 00:36:24.800
I don't necessarily love it or need it.

00:36:24.800 --> 00:36:25.810
I do it.

00:36:25.810 --> 00:36:27.140
Cause I wanna spend time with my kids now

00:36:27.140 --> 00:36:30.230
and things of that nature,
but it's a great question.

00:36:30.230 --> 00:36:32.470
Like to me, it's like you gotta

00:36:32.470 --> 00:36:34.750
really figure out who you are.

00:36:34.750 --> 00:36:37.320
Like, whatever I got, I
just have a ton of energy,

00:36:37.320 --> 00:36:38.960
cause I love what I'm doing and it just,

00:36:38.960 --> 00:36:40.741
you know, it's momentum right?

00:36:40.741 --> 00:36:42.770
But if tomorrow, I felt burnt out,

00:36:42.770 --> 00:36:44.230
like I'm not scared to take off.

00:36:44.230 --> 00:36:45.720
And I love like Christmas

00:36:45.720 --> 00:36:47.480
or the last two weeks of August

00:36:47.480 --> 00:36:48.820
when everyone's checked out,

00:36:48.820 --> 00:36:50.140
then I don't feel any anxiousness

00:36:50.140 --> 00:36:51.950
that somebody's getting
off on me, you know?

00:36:51.950 --> 00:36:53.120
To me, the problem is I feel like

00:36:53.120 --> 00:36:54.574
somebody's doing something and

00:36:54.574 --> 00:36:56.593
that competitive juice is kicking in.

00:36:56.593 --> 00:36:59.940
You know, I'm sure you feel
that with what you do, you know?

00:36:59.940 --> 00:37:02.530
If I'm not in the weight
room, somebody else is.

00:37:02.530 --> 00:37:03.983
You know and I feel that.

00:37:05.880 --> 00:37:07.211
I don't love it.

00:37:07.211 --> 00:37:09.640
I mean, the biggest
regret so far in my life

00:37:09.640 --> 00:37:10.990
is in my 20's, I did nothing.

00:37:10.990 --> 00:37:12.200
I worked every minute.

00:37:12.200 --> 00:37:13.277
I did nothing.

00:37:13.277 --> 00:37:15.500
And I could've taken a couple vacations.

00:37:15.500 --> 00:37:16.430
It would've been nice to hang out

00:37:16.430 --> 00:37:19.673
with my boys once in a while, I just, so.

00:37:22.190 --> 00:37:25.273
(low speaking voice)

00:37:29.890 --> 00:37:32.310
Well, one the Jets is not selling.

00:37:32.310 --> 00:37:34.740
I don't have two billion dollars yet.

00:37:34.740 --> 00:37:38.070
So, I'm not worried about
when he's gonna sell,

00:37:38.070 --> 00:37:40.570
or when he's not, I'm just
working on the process.

00:37:41.500 --> 00:37:43.500
I've had opportunities to invest.

00:37:43.500 --> 00:37:44.390
As a matter of fact, ironically,

00:37:44.390 --> 00:37:45.370
I had the opportunity to invest

00:37:45.370 --> 00:37:47.190
in the Dolphins with Steve Ross.

00:37:47.190 --> 00:37:48.420
Like, I've had some opportunities

00:37:48.420 --> 00:37:51.367
but I'm pretty focused on,
I wanna run it, you know?

00:37:51.367 --> 00:37:52.410
And I wanna be pit-less

00:37:52.410 --> 00:37:55.200
and I'm thrilled to buy the Jets at 74.

00:37:55.200 --> 00:37:58.540
Like if you said, that's what
it is, I'm like, amazing.

00:37:58.540 --> 00:37:59.373
You know?

00:37:59.373 --> 00:38:01.460
That's back to that patience.

00:38:01.460 --> 00:38:04.060
I need twenty, thirty more
years of wealth creation.

00:38:05.180 --> 00:38:06.590
Like a lot of people ask me why I'm

00:38:06.590 --> 00:38:08.080
running the business I run now,

00:38:08.080 --> 00:38:09.250
cause it's a crappy business,

00:38:09.250 --> 00:38:12.520
but I'm building the foundation
based on all my success.

00:38:12.520 --> 00:38:13.380
I love the process.

00:38:13.380 --> 00:38:14.720
I know what I'm building.

00:38:14.720 --> 00:38:15.730
Right?

00:38:15.730 --> 00:38:17.230
Like if I had your athletic ability,

00:38:17.230 --> 00:38:18.960
like I'd be in film room and weight room,

00:38:18.960 --> 00:38:20.700
I'd just be putting in the work.

00:38:20.700 --> 00:38:22.730
It's not complicated.

00:38:22.730 --> 00:38:25.290
You know what you have to do to get there.

00:38:25.290 --> 00:38:26.123
You know?

00:38:26.123 --> 00:38:27.950
You've got your talent, we all got it.

00:38:27.950 --> 00:38:29.420
The variable is the mindset of

00:38:29.420 --> 00:38:31.150
how much work you're gonna put in.

00:38:31.150 --> 00:38:32.300
Right?

00:38:32.300 --> 00:38:34.330
And the other thing is taking L's.

00:38:34.330 --> 00:38:37.200
I think most people don't
know how to take L's.

00:38:37.200 --> 00:38:40.629
And that's a huge part
of how I think about it.

00:38:40.629 --> 00:38:44.212
- [Coach] Last question
man, last question.

00:38:45.542 --> 00:38:46.425
- My guy.

00:38:46.425 --> 00:38:48.261
- [Audience Member] Did you buy a house?

00:38:48.261 --> 00:38:49.397
- Do I have a big house?

00:38:49.397 --> 00:38:50.810
Nope.

00:38:50.810 --> 00:38:51.643
Nope.

00:38:56.571 --> 00:38:58.079
- [Audience Member] How'd you get

00:38:58.079 --> 00:38:59.883
the confidence that you have now?

00:38:59.883 --> 00:39:02.413
- I think my mom over-loved me for sure.

00:39:03.250 --> 00:39:05.600
Like, just, she told
me I had it like that.

00:39:05.600 --> 00:39:09.973
And then, honestly, just, the
confidence came from losing.

00:39:11.070 --> 00:39:13.200
Believe it or not, you know?

00:39:13.200 --> 00:39:16.670
I think the biggest problem
we have in America right now,

00:39:16.670 --> 00:39:18.030
and we've got plenty of problems,

00:39:18.030 --> 00:39:22.108
but like, eighth place
trophies are fucking us up.

00:39:22.108 --> 00:39:22.963
You know?

00:39:24.183 --> 00:39:28.060
I got confidence from
taking a ton of losses.

00:39:28.060 --> 00:39:29.800
Cause then I figured
out what I was good at.

00:39:29.800 --> 00:39:32.690
I'd rather win and I
kept honing into that.

00:39:32.690 --> 00:39:34.390
But I wasn't scared to lose, you know?

00:39:34.390 --> 00:39:36.117
And that was it.

00:39:39.090 --> 00:39:39.923
Sneak one in?

00:39:40.770 --> 00:39:42.530
- [Audience Member] What do
you think is a good opportunity

00:39:42.530 --> 00:39:44.174
to invest our money into?

00:39:44.174 --> 00:39:45.234
- Amazon.

00:39:45.234 --> 00:39:46.780
- [Audience Member] Also,
with that being said,

00:39:46.780 --> 00:39:49.717
a lot of us, we've been trying
to think of ways as a team,

00:39:49.717 --> 00:39:51.680
you know with our scholarship
checks and things like that.

00:39:51.680 --> 00:39:53.540
A lot of us do realize that

00:39:53.540 --> 00:39:54.860
we won't be playing in the NFL,

00:39:54.860 --> 00:39:56.840
so we won't be making that
big money when we come out,

00:39:56.840 --> 00:39:58.500
so we're just trying to
set the foundation now,

00:39:58.500 --> 00:40:00.600
in the next four to five
years, to grow our money.

00:40:00.600 --> 00:40:02.210
As in, Coach Cochrane was talking about

00:40:02.210 --> 00:40:03.920
put a hundred dollars away each month,

00:40:03.920 --> 00:40:05.807
so that's 12 hundred dollars
at the end of the year.

00:40:05.807 --> 00:40:06.640
- I like that.

00:40:06.640 --> 00:40:07.812
- [Audience Member] Roll
it up and roll it up.

00:40:07.812 --> 00:40:09.140
What do you think is a smart opportunity

00:40:09.140 --> 00:40:11.477
for us to grow that money,
that we're putting away?

00:40:11.477 --> 00:40:12.310
- Amazon.

00:40:12.310 --> 00:40:13.663
- [Audience Member] A lot of
us don't have a lot of play.

00:40:13.663 --> 00:40:15.980
- Amazon.

00:40:15.980 --> 00:40:18.800
If you just put it into
Amazon, go to sleep,

00:40:18.800 --> 00:40:20.350
you'll be really happy with me.

00:40:21.670 --> 00:40:23.047
That's one, but I'm gonna
tell you something right now.

00:40:23.047 --> 00:40:26.450
I'm gonna wrap it up and put
a nice little bow tie on it.

00:40:26.450 --> 00:40:27.977
If they gave you a hundred
thousand dollars here

00:40:27.977 --> 00:40:29.380
and you put it away,

00:40:29.380 --> 00:40:31.213
that's nothing compared
to you leveraging the fact

00:40:31.213 --> 00:40:32.670
that you play for Bama football

00:40:32.670 --> 00:40:34.970
and you say hello to
everybody on this campus.

00:40:36.250 --> 00:40:37.200
Telling you right now man.

00:40:37.200 --> 00:40:38.400
That's the fucking game.

00:40:40.376 --> 00:40:41.503
Thank you so much for having me.

00:40:41.503 --> 00:40:44.503
(audience applause)

00:40:46.387 --> 00:40:47.720
Thank you Coach.

00:40:49.229 --> 00:40:52.396
